CHAPTER.VERS:
And it was so, that, after Yahweh had spoken these words to Job, Yahweh said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against you, and against your two companions; for you

          {+}
         have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my slave Job has.

Now therefore, take for yourselves seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my slave Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt-offering; and my slave Job will pray for you

          {+}
        ; for him I will accept, that I do not deal with you

          {+}
         after your

          {+}
         folly; for you

          {+}
         have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my slave Job has.
